### `333 moved`: saying that this node's directory was moved here, not copied.

moved-no-node = there is no node in { $root } to have moved.

moved-already-here = this node already lives at { $now }, so nothing was changed
    .keyword = home

moved-here = this node lives at { $now }, as you say.
    If a copy of this directory is still anywhere else, it is this name
    too: delete it rather than run it.
    .keyword = home
